{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:06:19.374448Z","id":"54a769cb632947576c432d669e6b68854052cff5af948918a8bc301aad480a49","body":{"detail":"clax_bin's fallback runs scripts/stable-bin.sh once per process, and under cargo nextest each test is a process: each one copies target/debug/clax (105 MB) and runs shasum on it, about 0.4 s unloaded. In clax-cli this replaces running CARGO_BIN_EXE_clax in place at no cost. A bare 'cargo nextest run -p clax-mcp -p clax-hooks -p clax-cli -p clax-fake-exe' took 77.8 s, with the clax-mcp channel tests at 18-27 s each against 8-12 s with CLAX_TEST_BIN set. just test and scripts/quality_gates.sh set CLAX_TEST_BIN, so they never take this path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"c2ccf3cc72fcfce5467fb8b524f98c127429d98d2c8b12c16a3126cea40ed637"},"suggested_fix":"Look up the kept copy by the source's size and modification time before copying, or have nextest set CLAX_TEST_BIN through a setup script.","summary":"Without CLAX_TEST_BIN, every test process copies and hashes the 105 MB debug clax","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:20:48.360341Z","id":"c75cd2f5010b9b6cedc4ec9bc691389258dc7c649d06683a1f7a2d876e632e07","body":{"detail":"cargo nextest run -p clax-fake-exe -p clax-cli -p clax-mcp -p clax-hooks -p clax-server on a 12-core machine with a load average of 6 to 9. With CLAX_TEST_BIN set, 1450 tests passed in 33.2 s. Without it, 1450 passed in 88.5 s. Mean time per test, with and then without: clax-cli 0.43 s and 1.12 s, clax-hooks 0.44 s and 7.0 s, clax-mcp channel 3.0 s and 14.9 s, clax-server 0.20 s and 0.30 s. clax-cli runs no cargo build, so its +0.7 s per test is all copying and hashing. One warm scripts/stable-bin.sh call takes 0.8 to 1.7 s (cp 0.14 s, shasum 0.27 s, the rest bash, ls and find). Twelve calls at once into an empty store finished at 3.6 to 11.0 s, against 0.7 to 1.3 s warm: each call makes and runs --version on its own new copy, and macOS assesses those copies one at a time. Fix: in clax_bin, before running stable-bin.sh, (1) hold std::fs::File::lock (safe std, stable since Rust 1.89; the toolchain is 1.94) on <store>/.lock, so only one process copies and assesses and the rest wait for it; (2) stat the source and look up <store>/by-stat/<dev>-<ino>-<size>-<mtime_ns>, a small file holding the kept path. If it exists and names an executable, return that path with no copy and no hash. Otherwise run stable-bin.sh, stat the source again, and only if the two stats match, write the pointer to a temporary file and rename it into place. Cargo replaces target/<profile>/clax with a new inode on every relink, so the key changes whenever the bytes do. The before/after check stops a relink during the copy from filing one build's bytes under another's key. No hard links (cp clones on APFS; rename is atomic). A nextest setup script that sets CLAX_TEST_BIN once per run would also remove the per-process cargo build that dominates clax-hooks, but it is experimental in the installed nextest 0.9.93 and does not help cargo test.","kind":"comment","references":"54a769cb632947576c432d669e6b68854052cff5af948918a8bc301aad480a49","summary":"Measured: a bare nextest run of the five affected crates takes 2.7x as long, and a cold build's copies are assessed one after another","tags":["review","severity:important","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:20:48.360432Z","id":"214d585b3c2c9d3854f8dacc84c390eca77507e5778cae022eb912be9170b860","body":{"detail":"Failure: CLAX_TEST_BIN=target/clax-bin/debug/<sha>/clax cargo nextest run -p clax-mcp -E 'test(a_session_ended_under_the_shim_is_replaced_on_the_next_publish)' panics at crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs:71 with 'CLAX_TEST_BIN .../crates/clax-mcp/target/clax-bin/debug/<sha>/clax missing'. Cargo and nextest start a test in its package directory, so absolute_from(bin, cwd) joins the path to crates/<name>/. AGENTS.md:56-58 recommends CLAX_TEST_BIN=\"$(scripts/stable-bin.sh target/debug/clax target/clax-bin/debug)\", and stable-bin.sh prints that path relative to the repository. Under Bazel, cwd is the runfiles root, which repo() also returns.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":73},"content_hash":"c396a15f77c6f7cf8c1ea2d0a49bad10f2453f46043600b705cfdabf96a5a90e"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve a relative CLAX_TEST_BIN against repo() instead of the current directory: the same result under Bazel, and the repository root under Cargo. Or add $PWD to the AGENTS.md command, as the justfile already does.","summary":"Under Cargo a relative CLAX_TEST_BIN resolves against the crate directory, so the form AGENTS.md documents fails","tags":["review","severity:minor","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:20:48.360471Z","id":"3f22409db7ef766a45978dfc7fe23cd32b5b15cff2cf9adc2c9366011874c64c","body":{"detail":"Failure: CLAX_TEST_BIN= cargo nextest run -p clax-mcp -E 'test(a_session_ended_under_the_shim_is_replaced_on_the_next_publish)' fails at crates/clax-mcp/tests/shim.rs:89 with 'spawn clax mcp: PermissionDenied', not with the 'CLAX_TEST_BIN … missing' message. absolute_from(\"\", cwd) returns cwd, a directory, and exists() is true for it. Before this change, PathBuf::from(\"\").exists() was false and the assert named the variable.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"20c4254a610e6876db65e16950827c4bb6aebf59ca45faf2f4203b459e226f0c"},"suggested_fix":"Treat an empty value as unset, or reject it, and check bin.is_file() instead of bin.exists().","summary":"An empty CLAX_TEST_BIN passes the existence check as the current directory","tags":["review","severity:minor","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:20:48.360506Z","id":"457918aeec9cd805092a2e22943c9a83c5861ec079d87a1cf5f2a6020b6f39ad","body":{"detail":"Changing line 69 to std::env::var_os(\"CLAX_TEST_BIN\").filter(|_| cargo_bin_exe.is_none()), so that clax-cli's tests ignore CLAX_TEST_BIN, still passes cargo test -p clax-fake-exe (6 passed), and CLAX_TEST_BIN=<kept copy> cargo nextest run -p clax-cli still passes (335 passed). The unit tests cover only repo_from and absolute_from. Under Bazel, CLAX_TEST_BIN winning is what keeps the cargo fallback from ever running (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-15-bazel-overlay-design.md §5.3, B14).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"c2ccf3cc72fcfce5467fb8b524f98c127429d98d2c8b12c16a3126cea40ed637"},"suggested_fix":"Split the choice into a pure function, choose(env_bin: Option<OsString>, cargo_bin_exe: Option<&str>, cwd, root) -> Source, and unit-test the precedence, relative paths and empty values.","summary":"No test checks which binary clax_bin chooses: a mutation that ignores CLAX_TEST_BIN in clax-cli passes everything","tags":["review","severity:minor","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:20:48.360533Z","id":"ea1d33146bbf2d18017ff48a9aa04d88c39557f7a1b72ee53013483906c12875","body":{"detail":"The behaviour comes from the five helpers this replaces. (1) After cargo nextest run --workspace --no-run, target/debug/clax hashed 70feb958…; cargo build -p clax-cli then relinked it to ffa3d070… (other dependency features), and the next workspace build compiled clax-cli again (9.9 s). In a bare workspace run, the first clax-mcp, clax-hooks or clax-server process's build swaps target/debug/clax, which is CARGO_BIN_EXE_clax. clax-cli tests that start before the swap run one build and later ones run the other. (2) The build is dev or release by cfg!(debug_assertions) and builds for the host, but the result is read from current_exe's <target>/<profile>/. With --target <triple> or a custom --cargo-profile, that directory is not where the build wrote, so the test fails, or silently runs an older binary left there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"d7a4de034acda606499cbc12b6965c53812c9608f864174eea6e1a3fe1f0b62a"},"suggested_fix":"Fold into the nextest-setup or single-build fix on 54a769cb; at least assert that the read binary is not older than the build's start.","summary":"The cargo fallback builds a binary with other features than the workspace test build, and can read a stale one under --target or a custom profile","tags":["review","severity:minor","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:13:41.482361Z","id":"1cdf5df08bf81d6d84be5ca1890cd878bd2eb6ab20fc5c0d81bc00ad410e5c2e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c0e42e1e","summary":"Fixed: keep() looks the kept copy up by a pointer <store>/by-stat/<dev>-<ino>-<size>-<mtime_ns> and runs stable-bin.sh once per build under an exclusive File::lock on <store>/.lock. 'cargo nextest run -p clax-fake-exe -p clax-cli -p clax-mcp -p clax-hooks -p clax-server' (load average 8-12): with CLAX_TEST_BIN 71.8 s; bare first run 88.9 s (it includes the fallback's cargo build of clax-cli, record ea1d3314's successor); bare second run 68.8 s; all 1456 passed each time.","supersedes":"54a769cb632947576c432d669e6b68854052cff5af948918a8bc301aad480a49","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:13:41.484433Z","id":"12b5868c86b3d918b398365d07b177a82e11aa59a7f928f0c27f5d81b8dd66ff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c0e42e1e","summary":"Fixed: choose() resolves a relative CLAX_TEST_BIN against repo(); test a_relative_clax_test_bin_is_against_the_repository_root passes (cargo test -p clax-fake-exe: 12 passed).","supersedes":"214d585b3c2c9d3854f8dacc84c390eca77507e5778cae022eb912be9170b860","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:13:41.486366Z","id":"de549e9ac33105800740cd2f4b2d3f1cf5a7fea1db935613d40e482ef84f0335","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c0e42e1e","summary":"Fixed: choose() treats an empty CLAX_TEST_BIN as unset and clax_bin asserts is_file(); test an_empty_clax_test_bin_counts_as_unset passes.","supersedes":"3f22409db7ef766a45978dfc7fe23cd32b5b15cff2cf9adc2c9366011874c64c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:13:41.488346Z","id":"0c8fda157445a2d66da2576040ee8b2c6c3892679f9140fc6b489147e88f0809","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c0e42e1e","summary":"Fixed: the choice is the pure function choose(), pinned by three tests. The mutation 'ignore CLAX_TEST_BIN when cargo_bin_exe is set' now fails a_set_clax_test_bin_wins_over_cargos_build and a_relative_clax_test_bin_is_against_the_repository_root (cargo test -p clax-fake-exe: 10 passed, 2 failed under the mutation).","supersedes":"457918aeec9cd805092a2e22943c9a83c5861ec079d87a1cf5f2a6020b6f39ad","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:13:41.490319Z","id":"c392fad6f7209f9d07393cc5269851bb9b82f48cfb661d466f8698acf22c9feb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c0e42e1e","summary":"Fixed for --target and custom profiles: cargo_build() builds with --target-dir set to the test executable's target directory and panics, naming CLAX_TEST_BIN, unless the test executable is in <target>/<debug|release>/deps with <target>/CACHEDIR.TAG. The feature difference is recorded on its own (the concern on cargo_build).","supersedes":"ea1d33146bbf2d18017ff48a9aa04d88c39557f7a1b72ee53013483906c12875","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:13:41.492236Z","id":"99d2c22e6d02cc53609d6a5cbc307da55636e5d7f764c25e14bcd03b42cc5ce8","body":{"detail":"cargo build -p clax-cli unifies features over clax-cli alone; a workspace test build unifies them with every crate's dev-dependencies, so the two clax binaries differ (hashes ffa3d070... and 70feb958... in one measurement). In a bare workspace run the first fallback build replaces CARGO_BIN_EXE_clax, so clax-cli tests may run either build, and the next workspace build recompiles clax-cli (about 10 s). Measured: the first bare run of the five clax-running crates took 88.9 s against 68.8 s for the second. The gates and Bazel set CLAX_TEST_BIN and never build here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":157},"content_hash":"885c19eaaaf632184d38d1682e2c524707007324cb4e4f86e8ab7242f8bb2e97"},"suggested_fix":"A nextest setup script that builds clax once and sets CLAX_TEST_BIN, once that feature is stable in the installed nextest.","summary":"The fallback's cargo build -p clax-cli relinks target/debug/clax with other dependency features than the workspace test build","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
